1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Okay, moving on to the adrenal gland.

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:05,280
Recall that the adrenal gland is actually two organs in one.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,920
There's an adrenal cortex,

4
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,860
which secretes hormones derived from cholesterol,

5
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,400
and then there is an adrenal medulla,

6
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,180
and the medulla, of course, secretes catecholamines,

7
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,980
such as epinephrine and norepinephrine.

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,840
We're going to begin our discussion with the adrenal cortex,

9
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,480
and then we're going to move on to the medulla.

10
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,660
Now, before we can discuss the cortex,

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,920
you need a little bit of background,

12
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:27,300
and so let's recall from histology

13
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,940
that the adrenal cortex actually has three layers,

14
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:34,280
a glomerulosa, a fasciculata, and a reticularis.

15
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,400
Now, that's pretty easy to remember.

16
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,120
One of the mnemonics that people like to use is GFR.

17
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,280
Remember that the adrenals sit on top of the kidney,

18
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,480
and, of course, in the kidney,

19
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:46,200
one of the key things that we always talk about is a GFR,

20
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:47,960
and so it shouldn't be hard to remember

21
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,360
that in the adrenal gland,

22
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,300
you're also going to think about GFR.

23
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:54,060
Again, glomerulosa, fasciculata, reticularis.

24
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,740
Now, you also need to remember

25
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:59,140
that all of the hormones that are produced by the cortex

26
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,980
are going to be derived from cholesterol.

27
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,080
In fact, if you recall from anatomy,

28
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,060
when you look at the adrenal,

29
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:05,780
it has a very distinct yellow color,

30
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,660
and that's because it's loaded with cholesterol,

31
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,420
which is eventually going to be used

32
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:10,560
to make all of these hormones.

33
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,920
Now, cholesterol in the glomerulosa

34
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:15,720
will eventually generate mineralocorticoids,

35
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,160
such as aldosterone,

36
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,720
and, of course, aldosterone is important

37
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:20,720
for salt maintenance.

38
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:25,760
Cholesterol will also eventually generate cortisol,

39
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,080
and cholesterol will also eventually generate

40
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,840
the sex steroids.

41
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:34,620
And one of the mnemonics that some students like to use

42
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:36,000
to remember this is, quote, unquote,

43
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,780
it gets sweeter as you get deeper,

44
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:40,680
i.e., this is salt, this is sugar,

45
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,420
because cortisol is important for maintaining sugar as well,

46
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,660
and this represents sex steroids.

47
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,460
And so I tell you that the adrenal gland

48
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,760
is composed of three layers,

49
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,080
glomerulosa, fasciculata, reticularis,

50
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:55,640
and, of course, the glomerulosa generates mineralocorticoids,

51
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:56,720
such as aldosterone.

52
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,440
The fasciculata generates glucocorticoids,

53
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,120
such as cortisol,

54
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,000
and the reticularis generates sex steroids.

55
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,540
The first disorder is Cushing syndrome,

56
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,820
and in Cushing syndrome, we have an excess of cortisol.

57
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,200
The clinical features of Cushing syndrome

58
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:13,100
will all be based on the physiology of cortisol.

59
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,880
One of the important things that cortisol does

60
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,160
is to raise the blood sugar,

61
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,960
and one way by which it does this

62
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,220
is to break down muscle for gluconeogenesis.

63
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,060
So patients with Cushing syndrome

64
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:26,420
are gonna have muscle weakness with thin extremities,

65
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:28,660
and, again, that's because you're breaking down muscle

66
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,860
to provide the amino acids necessary for gluconeogenesis.

67
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,660
In addition, the patients will have moon facies,

68
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,240
buffalo hump, and truncal obesity.

69
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:39,300
Now, the idea here is that if you have gluconeogenesis,

70
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,920
you're gonna have a high glucose in the blood.

71
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:43,680
The high glucose is gonna result in excess insulin

72
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,180
being produced by the pancreas.

73
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:48,340
The excess insulin will then result in the storage of fat,

74
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:50,540
and so fat will be stored in the face,

75
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,180
on the back, and on the trunk.

76
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,940
An additional consequence

77
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:57,240
is that the patients will develop abdominal striae.

78
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,420
The reason for this is that cortisol

79
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,140
impairs the synthesis of collagen,

80
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,920
and so when you have weak collagen,

81
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,560
the blood vessels can rupture easily,

82
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,780
and so you'll get these striae on the abdomen,

83
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:10,240
which basically represent ruptured blood vessels.

84
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:12,280
The patients can also develop hypertension.

85
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,020
The idea here is that cortisol upregulates

86
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,040
alpha-1 receptors on the arterioles,

87
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:19,820
which then increases the effect of norepinephrine.

88
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,320
Remember that cortisol is necessary for life,

89
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,780
and the reason it's necessary for life

90
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,760
is because it helps to maintain vascular tone,

91
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,880
and so the way by which it maintains vascular tone

92
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:32,840
is upregulation of alpha-1 receptors on arterioles,

93
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,680
and so when you have excess cortisol,

94
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,700
you'll have excess alpha-1 receptors,

95
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,540
which will then increase the effect of norepinephrine,

96
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:40,900
giving the patients hypertension.

97
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,780
That's particularly high yield.

98
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,300
The patients can also develop osteoporosis,

99
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,920
and finally, the patients can also get immune suppression,

100
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,500
and we're well aware of the fact

101
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,920
that cortisol is used as an immunosuppressant,

102
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,320
but it's important to go back and remind ourselves why,

103
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,060
and so there's three major mechanisms

104
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:58,680
by which cortisol results in immune suppression.

105
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:03,260
Number one is that it inhibits phospholipase A2,

106
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,160
and recall that if you inhibit phospholipase A2,

107
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,580
you won't be able to generate

108
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,420
your arachidonic acid metabolites,

109
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,520
and of course, those are essential for inflammation.

110
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,920
Number two is that it inhibits IL-2,

111
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:18,620
and IL-2 is an important T-cell growth factor,

112
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,340
and number three is that it inhibits

113
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:23,900
release of histamine from mast cells,

114
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,640
and of course, histamine is essential for vasodilation

115
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,620
and for increased vascular permeability,

116
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,700
and so all three of these are mechanisms

117
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:31,960
by which you get immune suppression

118
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,660
in patients with Cushing syndrome.

119
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,020
The diagnosis of Cushing syndrome

120
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,300
is made by detecting an increased

121
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:40,260
24-hour urine cortisol level,

122
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,780
and when you think about the causes of Cushing syndrome,

123
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,640
there's actually four major causes.

124
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,680
The first would be exogenous corticosteroids,

125
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:49,100
and so the idea here

126
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:52,280
is that we prescribed corticosteroids to the patient,

127
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:54,900
and as a result of that excess corticosteroids,

128
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,840
the patient will develop Cushing syndrome.

129
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,940
This is actually the most common cause

130
00:04:58,940 --> 00:04:59,820
of Cushing syndrome,

131
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:02,040
and one of the important consequences

132
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,080
with exogenous corticosteroids

133
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:06,460
is that both adrenal glands, in this case,

134
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:07,880
will actually become atrophic.

135
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,820
Now, let's just go back and remind ourselves.

136
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:12,220
When you have excess cortisol within the blood,

137
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:15,040
that cortisol will go to the anterior pituitary

138
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:17,040
and shut down the production of ACTH.

139
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,560
When you shut down the production of ACTH,

140
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,000
that's then gonna result

141
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,020
in both adrenal glands becoming small,

142
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,620
and so you'll have bilateral adrenal atrophy

143
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,540
with exogenous corticosteroids.

144
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:29,800
A second possible cause of Cushing syndrome

145
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,440
could be some adrenal problem.

146
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,940
For example, you can have an adenoma,

147
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,520
you can have hyperplasia,

148
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,320
or you can have a carcinoma within the adrenal,

149
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,020
and that could produce cortisol,

150
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,980
and so in this particular case,

151
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:42,700
what's going to happen,

152
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,940
the high cortisol obviously

153
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:45,020
would give you Cushing syndrome,

154
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:46,820
but what's gonna happen is

155
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,240
one adrenal will be big,

156
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:49,400
and this is, for example,

157
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,840
the adrenal gland that has the adenoma.

158
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,480
That adrenal is going to be secreting cortisol.

159
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,440
Cortisol will then go into the blood.

160
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:59,080
It'll then go and hit the anterior pituitary.

161
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,760
That'll shut down ACTH,

162
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,700
and when it shuts down ACTH,

163
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:06,180
the opposite adrenal will actually become atrophic,

164
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,180
and so one adrenal gland will be big,

165
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,940
i.e. the one that has, for example,

166
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:10,660
the adenoma,

167
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,260
and the other will be atrophic.

168
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,800
A third way by which we can develop Cushing syndrome

169
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,960
would be to have an ACTH-secreting pituitary adenoma.

170
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,580
Now, in this particular case,

171
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,560
what's going to happen is

172
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,120
that the adenoma and the pituitary

173
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,240
will secrete ACTH.

174
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,960
The ACTH will hit both adrenals

175
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,040
when it goes into the blood

176
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,680
and make both adrenals big.

177
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:32,000
Now, when both adrenals are hit by ACTH,

178
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:34,320
both adrenals will produce excess cortisol,

179
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,820
and that excess cortisol

180
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,600
will obviously result in Cushing syndrome.

181
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,220
The fourth possibility

182
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:42,120
is to have peroneoplastic ACTH secretion.

183
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,680
Now, in this particular case,

184
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,360
you have a tumor.

185
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:45,600
The most classic example

186
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,680
would be a small cell carcinoma of the lung.

187
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,660
The tumor secretes ACTH.

188
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,600
That ACTH goes into the blood.

189
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,340
It hits both adrenals.

190
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:54,820
When it hits both adrenals,

191
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:57,160
both adrenals will then become large,

192
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,540
and both adrenals will produce cortisol,

193
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,140
which will result in Cushing syndrome.

194
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:02,620
Now, notice that

195
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,400
when you look at these four possibilities,

196
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,580
this possibility is unique

197
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:07,980
in the sense that it's the only one

198
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:10,120
that gives you atrophy of both adrenals.

199
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,980
And this is unique

200
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,700
in the sense that you'd see one adrenal large

201
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,020
with a mass and the other adrenal atrophic.

202
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,940
However, when you look at these two,

203
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,940
you can't distinguish

204
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,660
based on the size of the adrenals.

205
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:23,980
And so you can actually do an additional test

206
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:24,880
to try to distinguish

207
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:27,280
an ACTH secreting pituitary adenoma

208
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,640
from ACTH secretion that arises

209
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:30,800
from, for example,

210
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,600
a small cell carcinoma of the lung.

211
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,420
And the way by which you do this

212
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,100
would be to do a high-dose

213
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,760
dexamethasone suppression test.

214
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,120
The idea here is that

215
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,840
when you give high-dose dexamethasone,

216
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,440
which is a cortisol analog,

217
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:43,940
it has the ability

218
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:45,800
to suppress ACTH production

219
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,180
by a pituitary adenoma.

220
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,100
However, it will not be able

221
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,880
to suppress ectopic ACTH production

222
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,780
by a small cell carcinoma of the lung.

223
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,180
The way I think about this

224
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:56,900
is sort of the high-dose dexamethasone

225
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:57,740
gets into the blood,

226
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,820
it goes up to the pituitary adenoma,

227
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,820
and it slaps the pituitary adenoma

228
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:02,680
and says, wake up,

229
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,620
you're actually still

230
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,600
a benign pituitary cell.

231
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,520
And so then the pituitary adenoma

232
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,780
responds by shutting down

233
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,020
its ACTH production.

234
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:12,240
However, when high-dose dexamethasone

235
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,820
goes up to the small cell carcinoma

236
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:14,660
of the lung and tries

237
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,080
to slap it back into shape,

238
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,880
the small cell carcinoma of the lung

239
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:18,920
just slaps it back

240
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,060
because it is a cancer.

241
00:08:20,420 --> 00:08:21,680
It is not going to listen to

242
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:22,760
or respond to anyone.

243
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:23,780
And so therefore,

244
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:25,000
high-dose dexamethasone

245
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,240
will not shut down ACTH production

246
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,900
by the small cell carcinoma

247
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:29,400
of the lung.

248
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,760
The final point is that

249
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,480
when you do this

250
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,520
high-dose dexamethasone suppression test,

251
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:35,400
you'll actually follow the effect

252
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,860
by measuring cortisol levels.

253
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,260
So the dexamethasone

254
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:39,480
will then decrease

255
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,660
the ACTH production

256
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:42,060
by the adenoma, for example,

257
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,420
which will then decrease

258
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,360
the amount of cortisol

259
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:45,100
being produced,

260
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,100
and so you'll be able

261
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,160
to detect decreased cortisol levels.

262
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:49,900
Hyper-aldosteronism

263
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,740
is when you have excess aldosterone,

264
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,780
and the effects of excess aldosterone

265
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,600
will all be based

266
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,920
on the normal physiology

267
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:56,720
of aldosterone.

268
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,000
So let's go back

269
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:58,980
and just remind ourselves

270
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,140
before we go to the text

271
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:02,600
that aldosterone works

272
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,380
on the late distal tubule

273
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:05,560
and the collecting duct.

274
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:06,840
And in this region,

275
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,180
there are two main cell types.

276
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,000
There is the principal cell

277
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
and there is

278
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,980
the alpha-intercalated cell.

279
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,400
Now the principal cell

280
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,720
in response to aldosterone

281
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,400
will actually grab sodium

282
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:20,440
and will dump potassium.

283
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,540
And the alpha-intercalated cell

284
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:25,060
in response to aldosterone

285
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:27,520
will actually dump hydrogen ion.

286
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,320
And so now you can imagine

287
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:29,960
that if a patient

288
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,200
has hyperaldosteronism,

289
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:32,400
they're going to get

290
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:33,660
hypernatremia

291
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,020
because they're grabbing sodium,

292
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,060
they're going to get

293
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:36,980
hypokalemia

294
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:38,940
because they're dumping potassium,

295
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,220
and they're going to get

296
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:41,780
a metabolic alkalosis

297
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,980
because they're dumping hydrogen ion.

298
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,800
And so this is the key findings,

299
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,080
as I've stated here in the text.

300
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:48,420
I say that the presentation

301
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,600
is hypernatremia,

302
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:50,620
you're grabbing sodium,

303
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,740
hypokalemia,

304
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,000
you're dumping potassium,

305
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,900
and a metabolic acidosis

306
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,240
because you're dumping hydrogen ion.

307
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:57,180
Now of course,

308
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:58,740
the patients will also have hypertension,

309
00:09:59,340 --> 00:09:59,980
and that's because

310
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:00,980
when you grab sodium,

311
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,200
water is going to follow,

312
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,200
which is going to raise

313
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:03,940
the blood volume.

314
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:06,240
In primary hyperaldosteronism,

315
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,660
the high aldosterone

316
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:09,220
is due to a primary problem

317
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:10,300
within the adrenal gland,

318
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:11,700
and this would most commonly

319
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,160
be due to a benign tumor

320
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:13,980
of the adrenal gland

321
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,440
called an adrenal adenoma.

322
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,900
It is also possible

323
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:18,980
to have primary hyperaldosteronism

324
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:20,780
due to hyperplasia

325
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:21,860
or carcinoma

326
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:22,800
of the adrenal gland.

327
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:23,320
However,

328
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:25,040
these are much less common causes.

329
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:26,620
Now in this particular case,

330
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,980
you're going to have a high aldosterone

331
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:29,080
because you've got primary

332
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,300
hyperaldosteronism,

333
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,300
and you're going to have

334
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,080
a low renin.

335
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,080
Now recall that

336
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:34,360
when you have high aldosterone,

337
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,380
you're going to grab sodium,

338
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,400
and water is going to follow,

339
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,180
and that's going to raise

340
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:37,880
the blood volume.

341
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,240
That high blood volume

342
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,120
is then going to go

343
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:40,900
to the kidney,

344
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,040
so the kidney is going

345
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,160
to see high blood flow,

346
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,100
and so therefore,

347
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,080
it will decrease

348
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,400
the production of renin,

349
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,480
and so you'll have

350
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,240
a low renin,

351
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,020
and that's particularly high yield

352
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:50,760
when thinking about

353
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,400
primary hyperaldosteronism.

354
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,780
In secondary hyperaldosteronism,

355
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:56,200
you get a high aldosterone,

356
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:56,540
however,

357
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,020
it's secondary to the fact

358
00:10:58,020 --> 00:10:59,360
that you have activated

359
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,400
the renin-angiotensin system.

360
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:02,560
Now recall from

361
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:03,620
our vascular lectures

362
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,880
that if this is the aorta,

363
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,040
and this is the renal artery,

364
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:06,960
and this is the kidney,

365
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:08,040
there's a couple ways

366
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:09,080
by which this could occur.

367
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:09,980
Classically,

368
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:10,800
in a young woman,

369
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:11,640
you can get something

370
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,280
called fibromuscular dysplasia,

371
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,840
which results in thickening

372
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,020
of the wall of the blood vessel,

373
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,260
which would then decrease

374
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,360
the blood flow to the kidney,

375
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:19,920
and therefore activate

376
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:21,320
the juxtaglomerular apparatus,

377
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,560
or you could get atherosclerosis,

378
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,560
particularly in elderly males,

379
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,000
which would then decrease

380
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,020
the blood flow to the kidney,

381
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,240
also activating

382
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:30,920
the juxtaglomerular apparatus.

383
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,560
Now recall from physiology

384
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,380
that when you activate

385
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:34,080
the JGA,

386
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,720
or the juxtaglomerular apparatus,

387
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:36,820
you're going to then

388
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,560
secrete renin,

389
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:38,560
so you're going to have

390
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:39,500
a high renin.

391
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:40,160
Of course,

392
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,140
the renin converts

393
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:42,160
angiotensinogen

394
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,440
to angiotensin 1.

395
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,780
Angiotensin 1

396
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:45,640
then gets converted

397
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,460
by angiotensin-converting enzyme

398
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:48,640
to angiotensin 2,

399
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,460
and then angiotensin 2

400
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,280
goes to the adrenal gland

401
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,620
and causes release

402
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:55,260
of aldosterone.

403
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,020
And so you're going

404
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,120
to have high aldosterone

405
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,120
because of the fact

406
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:58,860
that you activated

407
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:00,720
the renin-angiotensin system.

408
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:03,080
Congenital adrenal hyperplasia

409
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,800
is when you have hyperplasia

410
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,100
of both adrenal glands

411
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,260
due to a congenital defect

412
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:09,660
in the enzymes necessary

413
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,900
for steroidogenesis.

414
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,620
The most common deficiency

415
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:14,540
is a 21-hydroxylase deficiency.

416
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,340
However,

417
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,580
before you can understand this,

418
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,300
we need to go back

419
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,020
to the whiteboard.

420
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,660
Remember that cholesterol

421
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:21,320
is the starting point

422
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,880
for steroidogenesis

423
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:24,060
in the adrenal cortex.

424
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,260
It gets converted

425
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,340
to pregnenolone,

426
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:28,500
and pregnenolone

427
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,160
can enter into

428
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,180
one of three pathways.

429
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,620
It can produce

430
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,180
mineralocorticoids,

431
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,620
it can produce

432
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:35,500
cortisol,

433
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,080
or it can eventually

434
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,360
produce sex steroids.

435
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:40,140
Now,

436
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:40,740
in order to produce

437
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:41,720
mineralocorticoids,

438
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:43,240
you need 21-hydroxylase,

439
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:44,500
and in order to produce

440
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:44,920
cortisol,

441
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,580
you need 21-hydroxylase.

442
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:47,580
Imagine,

443
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,460
if there's a deficiency

444
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,920
of 21-hydroxylase

445
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:50,640
here and here,

446
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:51,940
then pregnenolone

447
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:52,680
will be shunted

448
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:54,780
to the preferential production

449
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:55,720
of sex steroids,

450
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:57,320
and so the sex steroids

451
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,100
will increase.

452
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:58,840
Now,

453
00:12:58,880 --> 00:12:59,780
the consequence of this

454
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:00,440
is that the patient

455
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,860
can get clitoral enlargement

456
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:02,580
if they're a female,

457
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:03,780
or they can get

458
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,560
precocious puberty

459
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:05,240
if they're a male.

460
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:06,460
In addition,

461
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:07,760
there's going to be

462
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,800
a lack of cortisol

463
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:09,580
because you can't

464
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:10,280
produce cortisol.

465
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:11,740
This will result

466
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:12,620
in decreased cortisol

467
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:13,140
in the blood,

468
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:14,360
and the decreased cortisol

469
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:14,840
in the blood

470
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,640
can result in,

471
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,240
number one,

472
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,820
life-threatening hypotension,

473
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:18,960
because remember

474
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:19,520
that cortisol

475
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,900
is necessary for life,

476
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:21,920
and in particular,

477
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:22,980
it helps to maintain

478
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,020
vascular tone,

479
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:25,120
and so you can get

480
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,360
life-threatening hypotension,

481
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:27,320
and number two,

482
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:27,900
because you have

483
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:28,680
decreased cortisol,

484
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,260
you're going to have

485
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:31,000
decreased inhibitory feedback

486
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,400
on the anterior pituitary,

487
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:33,460
so there'll be

488
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:34,400
excess production

489
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,120
of ACTH.

490
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,020
The excess ACTH

491
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,040
will get into the blood,

492
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,480
it'll hit both adrenals

493
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,680
and make both adrenals

494
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:41,040
big,

495
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:41,740
and in fact,

496
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:42,680
that's why we call it

497
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,440
congenital adrenal hyperplasia.

498
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:46,380
Now, the third consequence

499
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,820
of having this defect

500
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,000
of 21-hydroxylase

501
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:49,780
will be that you won't

502
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:51,120
have mineralocorticoids.

503
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:52,260
When there's a loss

504
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:52,980
of aldosterone,

505
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:53,600
for example,

506
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:54,880
you'll get salt wasting.

507
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:55,880
Now, remember that

508
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:56,820
aldosterone normally

509
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:57,560
grabs salt

510
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,740
and dumps potassium,

511
00:13:59,220 --> 00:14:00,180
so if you're lacking

512
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:01,060
aldosterone,

513
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,040
you're actually going

514
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,340
to lose salt,

515
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,340
i.e. salt wasting,

516
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:04,920
and you're going

517
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:06,100
to hold potassium,

518
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,340
and so the patients

519
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,220
will actually get

520
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:10,180
salt wasting

521
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,360
with hyponatremia

522
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,860
and hyperkalemia

523
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,360
because they're

524
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,160
holding potassium.

525
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,560
And at the same time,

526
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,960
normally because sodium

527
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:17,640
would come in

528
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,860
and water would follow,

529
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:19,980
in this case,

530
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:20,500
you're not going

531
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,520
to be bringing back sodium,

532
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:22,260
and so you're not

533
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:22,820
going to be bringing

534
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:23,440
back water,

535
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:24,380
and so the patients

536
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:25,160
can also become

537
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:26,040
hypovolemic.

538
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:27,300
Now, with this background

539
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:27,660
in mind,

540
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,260
let's go back

541
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:28,860
to the text.

542
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:38,540
Reduction of sex steroids

543
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:40,220
and the fact that

544
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:40,980
there'll be a deficiency

545
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:41,660
of cortisol

546
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,160
will lead to increased

547
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,500
ACTH from the anterior

548
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,160
pituitary.

549
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:46,200
Again, you're lacking

550
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,260
feedback on the anterior

551
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:47,900
pituitary,

552
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:48,980
which is then going

553
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:50,140
to result in bilateral

554
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,360
adrenal hyperplasia.

555
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:52,820
The clinical features

556
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:54,000
will be salt wasting.

557
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:55,660
Again, lack of aldosterone,

558
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,080
so you can't grab salt,

559
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:57,940
so you'll waste it

560
00:14:57,940 --> 00:14:59,300
and you'll get hyponatremia

561
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:00,960
and you'll have hyperkalemia.

562
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:02,340
Again, normally aldosterone

563
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,280
would dump potassium,

564
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:03,800
but you're going

565
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,900
to hold potassium,

566
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:06,620
and there'll be hypovolemia

567
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,240
because you're not

568
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,080
bringing in salt.

569
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:09,280
There'll also be

570
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,580
life-threatening hypotension

571
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:11,980
because of the low cortisol,

572
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,080
and finally,

573
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:13,940
the patients can have

574
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:14,900
clitoral enlargement

575
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:15,760
if they're a female

576
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:16,880
or precocious puberty

577
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:17,520
in a male,

578
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:18,460
and that's because

579
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,160
of the increased

580
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:19,920
sex steroids.

581
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:21,140
Now, I'd like to actually

582
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:22,320
take this one step further,

583
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,660
although your text doesn't,

584
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,120
just to add a couple things

585
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,820
because it's easy

586
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:27,540
to do so here

587
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:28,160
and they're potentially

588
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:28,760
high-yield.

589
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,240
Let's just remind ourselves

590
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:30,940
that cholesterol

591
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:32,180
is a starting point

592
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:33,240
of steroidogenesis.

593
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,320
It can result

594
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,120
in the production

595
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,320
of pregnenolone,

596
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,620
and pregnenolone

597
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:38,780
can eventually enter

598
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:40,280
into one of three pathways.

599
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,320
It can lead

600
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,040
to the production

601
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,360
of mineralocorticoids

602
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,280
or cortisol

603
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,040
or sex steroids.

604
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,460
In order to produce cortisol,

605
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:48,200
you need both

606
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,400
21-hydroxylase

607
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,620
and 11-hydroxylase.

608
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:51,940
In order to produce

609
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,260
weak mineralocorticoids,

610
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,760
you need 21-hydroxylase,

611
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,100
and in order to produce

612
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:56,880
the next level

613
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:57,940
of mineralocorticoids,

614
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,420
you need 11-hydroxylase.

615
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,740
This is important

616
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,640
because remember,

617
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:03,580
when you lose 21-hydroxylase,

618
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:04,400
you don't produce

619
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,500
mineralocorticoids

620
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,920
and you don't produce

621
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:07,580
any cortisol,

622
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:08,700
and so the patients

623
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,540
have salt wasting

624
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,500
with all the symptoms

625
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,500
that I've already described.

626
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:12,220
However,

627
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:13,260
imagine if you had

628
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:14,860
an 11-hydroxylase deficiency.

629
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,560
You'd also not be able

630
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,560
to produce cortisol,

631
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:18,840
and you'd also get

632
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,500
some shunting

633
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,000
towards sex steroids.

634
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:21,720
However,

635
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,560
you would produce

636
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,280
a little bit

637
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:25,060
of a weak mineralocorticoid,

638
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,000
and so you wouldn't

639
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:26,900
have the salt wasting.

640
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:28,440
And so on board examination,

641
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:29,120
if they give you

642
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,180
the classic history

643
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:30,860
of someone with

644
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,360
a 21-hydroxylase deficiency,

645
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:33,260
however,

646
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:34,340
the patient doesn't

647
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,160
have salt wasting

648
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,460
and doesn't have

649
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:37,280
hyperkalemia

650
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,360
and doesn't have

651
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,240
hypovolemia,

652
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,260
then you need to remember

653
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:42,120
that it's not

654
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,320
a 21-hydroxylase,

655
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:43,940
but instead,

656
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:46,200
it's an 11-hydroxylase problem,

657
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:47,420
and that's particularly

658
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:47,980
high yield,

659
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:48,800
so I'm taking a minute

660
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,080
to just explain that to you.

661
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,580
Cortisol and sex steroids,

662
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:03,560
you need 17-hydroxylase.

663
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:04,540
Now imagine,

664
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:05,140
if you're lacking

665
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:06,560
17-hydroxylase,

666
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:07,480
then you won't be able

667
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,400
to produce anything

668
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,120
on this side,

669
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,180
and the only thing

670
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:10,980
that you're going to produce

671
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:13,160
is excess mineralocorticoids,

672
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:14,200
and so if there's

673
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,840
a 17-hydroxylase deficiency,

674
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:16,900
the problem will be

675
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,940
excess mineralocorticoids

676
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:20,040
with no cortisol

677
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,460
and no sex steroids.

678
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:22,680
Now notice one thing,

679
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:23,200
and that is that

680
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,220
in all of these deficiencies,

681
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,600
17, 21, and 11,

682
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:26,800
you're always not

683
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:27,680
producing cortisol,

684
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:28,820
and so because you're

685
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:30,160
always not producing cortisol,

686
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:31,200
you're always going

687
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,040
to have excess ACTH

688
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:34,080
because of a lack

689
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:34,520
of feedback,

690
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:36,280
and so each of these cases

691
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:37,120
would result in

692
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:39,280
congenital adrenal hyperplasia.

693
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,060
Adrenal insufficiency

694
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:41,580
is when you have

695
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:42,760
a lack of adrenal hormones,

696
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:43,840
and adrenal insufficiency

697
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,140
can actually occur acutely

698
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,660
or can occur chronically.

699
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,020
When it's acute,

700
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,820
the classic high yield example

701
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:51,800
is Waterhouse-Friedrichsen syndrome.

702
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,520
This classically arises

703
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,520
in a young child

704
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:56,600
with a Neisseria meningitis infection

705
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,180
who develops DIC

706
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:00,900
and then gets bilateral necrosis

707
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,140
of both adrenal glands,

708
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:03,040
and of course,

709
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:03,840
that then results

710
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:05,320
in an acute lack of cortisol.

711
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:06,820
The acute lack of cortisol

712
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:08,740
would then exacerbate

713
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:09,900
the patient's hypotension.

714
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:10,740
Now, of course,

715
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:11,300
they've already got

716
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:12,900
Neisseria meningitis and DIC,

717
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,440
however, on top of that,

718
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,120
they then get this massive hypotension

719
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:17,240
due to a lack of cortisol,

720
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,420
and so this is particularly high yield.

721
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,340
Now here's a classic example.

722
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,180
Notice that this is

723
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:23,280
the adrenal gland here,

724
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:24,420
and you can see

725
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:25,400
that this adrenal gland

726
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,140
has been converted

727
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:27,500
to a sack of blood,

728
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,160
and that's the classic image

729
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:29,940
that they like to show.

730
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:30,920
It's a very common image

731
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,260
that shows up on board exams,

732
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:33,900
so the sack of blood adrenal,

733
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,480
and this again represents

734
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,960
Waterhouse-Friedrichsen syndrome

735
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:37,660
classically.

736
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:39,260
Chronic insufficiency

737
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,040
is when you get

738
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,820
slow progressive destruction

739
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:42,940
of the adrenal glands,

740
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:44,640
and there are three major causes

741
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,460
that are high yield

742
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,260
for the board exam.

743
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,700
The first is autoimmune destruction.

744
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:50,480
This is the most common cause

745
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,080
in the West.

746
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,240
The second is when

747
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,840
there's destruction of the adrenal glands

748
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:54,420
by TB,

749
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:56,340
and this is the most common cause

750
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,460
in the developing world,

751
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:58,740
and the third

752
00:18:58,740 --> 00:19:00,980
is when there is metastatic carcinoma

753
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:03,160
that metastasizes to both adrenals,

754
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:05,340
and this is a very common cause

755
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:06,180
on board exams,

756
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:08,280
and the particular example here

757
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,220
that you want to bear in mind

758
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,640
is that lung cancer

759
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:12,120
loves to go to the adrenal,

760
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,240
very high yield.

761
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,560
Lung cancer

762
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,000
loves to go to the adrenal.

763
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,380
Now the clinical features

764
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,440
of chronic insufficiency

765
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,360
are going to be based

766
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:21,220
on a lack of the hormones

767
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:22,700
normally produced by the adrenal.

768
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,480
So you're going to get hypotension.

769
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:24,800
Why?

770
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:25,960
Because you don't have cortisol,

771
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:27,440
and cortisol is necessary

772
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:28,940
to maintain vascular tone.

773
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:31,240
You're going to get hyponatremia,

774
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,480
hypovolemia,

775
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,640
and hyperkalemia.

776
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:35,600
Again, you don't have aldosterone.

777
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:37,220
Aldosterone normally grabs sodium,

778
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,420
so because you don't have it,

779
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,420
you're going to dump sodium.

780
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,860
Aldosterone normally dumps potassium.

781
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:42,800
Because you don't have it,

782
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,340
you're going to hold potassium,

783
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:46,540
and because you don't have sodium,

784
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,440
you're also going to lose volume.

785
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:50,800
Patients can also get hyperpigmentation,

786
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:52,200
the idea here is that

787
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,280
if you don't have cortisol,

788
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,220
you're not going to be able

789
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:56,000
to negatively shut down

790
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,600
the production of ACTH

791
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:59,060
by the anterior pituitary,

792
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,720
so there'll be excess production

793
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,380
of ACTH.

794
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,560
Now ACTH is actually derived

795
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,760
from a molecule called POMC,

796
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,560
and one of the derivatives

797
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:11,500
of POMC is melanocyte-simulating hormone,

798
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:13,080
which will then stimulate

799
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:13,820
the melanocytes,

800
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,400
resulting in hyperpigmentation,

801
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,900
and it classically arises

802
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:18,360
in the oral mucosa,

803
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:19,480
but it'll also be present

804
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,080
on the skin.

805
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:21,220
And then the patients

806
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,160
also have vomiting and diarrhea,

807
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,640
again, due to a lack of cortisol.

808
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,980
Moving on to the adrenal medulla,

809
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,360
recall that the adrenal medulla

810
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:30,100
is composed of chromophane cells,

811
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:31,780
very high yield for board exams.

812
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:32,620
These are derived

813
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:33,580
from the neural crest.

814
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,700
They are the main physiologic source

815
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:36,620
of catecholamines,

816
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,860
and so both epinephrine

817
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:38,800
and norepinephrine

818
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,760
are released by the adrenal medulla.

819
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,260
The key pathology

820
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,080
that we want to cover

821
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,900
is called a pheochromocytoma.

822
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:46,280
A pheochromocytoma

823
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,300
is when you have a tumor

824
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,600
of the chromophane cells.

825
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:49,880
Now, when you get a tumor

826
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,880
of the chromophane cells,

827
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:52,300
the classic finding

828
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:53,260
on gross exam

829
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,440
and very high yield to know

830
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,980
is that you get a brown tumor.

831
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,100
Now, that's because

832
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:58,540
the adrenal medulla is brown,

833
00:20:58,860 --> 00:20:59,480
and so if you get

834
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,960
this big tumor here

835
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,180
of the adrenal medulla,

836
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:02,740
of course,

837
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:03,520
it's also going to have

838
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,200
the same color,

839
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:04,900
which is brown.

840
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,060
Now, notice here

841
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,900
that you see this little yellow line

842
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:09,220
running along the edge

843
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:09,720
of the tumor,

844
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:10,700
and do you know what that is?

845
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,240
That little yellow line

846
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,580
represents the adrenal cortex.

847
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:14,740
And, of course,

848
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:15,580
the adrenal cortex

849
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,580
has a yellow color

850
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:17,880
because it's loaded

851
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:18,640
with cholesterol,

852
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,240
which is the starting point

853
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,660
for the production of steroids.

854
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:23,520
The clinical features

855
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,760
of pheochromocytoma

856
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:26,460
will be episodic hypertension,

857
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:28,880
headaches, palpitations,

858
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:30,240
tachycardia, and sweating.

859
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,880
All of these are a consequence

860
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:33,940
of epinephrine and norepinephrine.

861
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,460
The diagnosis is made

862
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:36,100
by detecting

863
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,840
increased serum metanephrines

864
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:40,100
and increased 24-hour urine

865
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,480
metanephrines in VMA.

866
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:42,800
Now, let's go back

867
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,440
to biochemistry

868
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,240
and remind ourselves

869
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,460
that if you have epinephrine

870
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:47,020
and norepinephrine,

871
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:48,440
the epinephrine

872
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:49,820
will be broken down

873
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:51,520
into metanephrine,

874
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,680
and the norepinephrine

875
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,780
will be broken down

876
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:57,580
into normetanephrine.

877
00:21:58,580 --> 00:21:59,340
These two,

878
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:00,160
both metanephrine

879
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:01,220
and norepinephrine,

880
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:02,540
will be broken down

881
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:04,140
into VMA.

882
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:05,180
And, of course,

883
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:06,260
the enzyme that does this

884
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:08,740
is monoamine oxidase.

885
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,140
Now, this is particularly

886
00:22:10,140 --> 00:22:11,260
high-yield biochemistry

887
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:12,380
because, of course,

888
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:13,360
if you've got a tumor

889
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:13,980
that's producing

890
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:15,380
epinephrine and norepinephrine,

891
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,640
then one way by which

892
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,700
you can make the diagnosis

893
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:18,780
is to detect

894
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:20,480
increased metanephrines

895
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,340
or increased VMA.

896
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:23,780
And so that's what we're saying

897
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:24,460
here in the text.

898
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,520
Let's go back to the book.

899
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:27,560
Diagnosed by increased

900
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:29,020
serum metanephrines

901
00:22:29,020 --> 00:22:31,420
and increased 24-hour urine

902
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:33,040
metanephrines and VMA.

903
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:33,760
So, again,

904
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:35,060
that's particularly high-yield.

905
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:36,160
Now, the treatment

906
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:37,180
is surgical excision.

907
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:38,640
However, it's very high-yield

908
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,600
to know for the purposes

909
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:40,400
of board exams

910
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,620
that before you remove

911
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:42,020
the tumor,

912
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:42,540
you're going to give

913
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:43,080
the patient's

914
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,080
phenoxybenzamine,

915
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,700
which is an irreversible

916
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:46,980
blocker of alpha receptors.

917
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:48,280
Now, the idea here

918
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,140
is that when the surgeon

919
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:50,400
goes in to remove the tumor,

920
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:51,860
if they grab the tumor,

921
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,780
when they squeeze it,

922
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:53,940
they could actually squeeze out

923
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:55,240
epinephrine and norepinephrine.

924
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:57,060
That can result in massive

925
00:22:57,060 --> 00:22:58,420
hypertension in the patient

926
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:00,200
and can actually result in death.

927
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:01,560
And so, in order to avoid

928
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:02,760
the effect of this surge

929
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:04,120
of epinephrine and norepinephrine,

930
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:05,000
patients are given

931
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,040
phenoxybenzamine

932
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:07,660
before the tumor is removed.

933
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,020
Additional features

934
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:09,980
of pheochromocytoma

935
00:23:09,980 --> 00:23:10,580
are remembered

936
00:23:10,580 --> 00:23:11,840
by the rules of 10.

937
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:13,380
10% are bilateral,

938
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:15,040
10% are familial,

939
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:16,780
10% are malignant,

940
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,860
i.e. 90% are benign,

941
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:20,380
and 10% are located

942
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:21,980
outside of the adrenal medulla.

943
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:23,280
Now, it's very high yield

944
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:24,960
to note that one classic location

945
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,260
outside of the adrenal medulla

946
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:27,440
would be the bladder wall.

947
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:28,820
And so, on a board exam,

948
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:29,620
if you have a patient

949
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:30,760
that when they urinate

950
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:32,360
develops episodic hypertension,

951
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:33,100
et cetera,

952
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:35,360
think about a pheochromocytoma

953
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,680
involving the wall

954
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:37,540
of the bladder.

955
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:38,200
And again,

956
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:38,960
that's particularly

957
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:39,980
high yield as well.

958
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:41,620
Now, a few associations

959
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:42,700
with pheochromocytoma

960
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:43,960
to close off this discussion.

961
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:45,140
The first is that

962
00:23:45,140 --> 00:23:46,780
patients with both MEN2A

963
00:23:46,780 --> 00:23:47,860
and MEN2B

964
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,360
can develop pheochromocytoma.

965
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,500
Just as a review

966
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,800
from earlier in this section,

967
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,360
remember that MEN2A

968
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,020
is medullary carcinoma

969
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:55,640
of the thyroid,

970
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:56,960
pheochromocytoma,

971
00:23:57,220 --> 00:23:58,500
and parathyroid adenoma.

972
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,140
And that MEN2B

973
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:01,400
is medullary carcinoma

974
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,100
of the thyroid,

975
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:03,780
pheochromocytoma,

976
00:24:04,220 --> 00:24:06,340
and mucosal ganglioneuromas,

977
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:08,240
especially in the oral mucosa.

978
00:24:08,740 --> 00:24:09,760
Now, also remember

979
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:10,920
from earlier in this section

980
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:11,980
that the key thing

981
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:13,540
about MEN2 overall

982
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:15,140
is that medullary carcinoma

983
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:15,800
of the thyroid

984
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:16,560
is the key thing

985
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:17,520
that would kill the patient.

986
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:18,500
And so one way

987
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:19,580
we can avoid developing

988
00:24:19,580 --> 00:24:20,080
the cancer

989
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:20,800
would be to remove

990
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,300
the thyroid.

991
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:22,500
And remember that

992
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,320
there's a key gene

993
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:24,340
that you want to test for

994
00:24:24,340 --> 00:24:25,580
before you remove the thyroid

995
00:24:25,580 --> 00:24:26,260
to determine

996
00:24:26,260 --> 00:24:27,280
if there's a genetic risk.

997
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:28,020
And what's that gene?

998
00:24:28,520 --> 00:24:28,820
RET.

999
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:30,180
Again, the association

1000
00:24:30,180 --> 00:24:31,040
of RET mutation

1001
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:32,400
leading to medullary carcinoma

1002
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:32,940
of the thyroid

1003
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:34,060
is very high yield

1004
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:34,820
for board exams.

1005
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:36,620
Von Hippel-Lindau disease

1006
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:38,400
is an autosomal dominant condition

1007
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:38,980
where you lose

1008
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:39,840
the von Hippel-Lindau

1009
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:40,800
tumor suppressor gene.

1010
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,920
We talked about this disease

1011
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,820
in the renal section.

1012
00:24:43,300 --> 00:24:44,120
Remember that the patients

1013
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:45,000
have an increased risk

1014
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,140
of hemangioblastoma

1015
00:24:46,140 --> 00:24:47,040
of the cerebellum

1016
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:48,260
and an increased risk

1017
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:49,440
of renal cell carcinoma

1018
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,460
and now I'm telling you

1019
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:52,540
that there's an increased risk

1020
00:24:52,540 --> 00:24:53,620
of pheochromocytoma

1021
00:24:53,620 --> 00:24:54,740
in those patients as well.

1022
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:55,700
And finally,

1023
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,380
in neurofibromatosis type 1,

1024
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:58,940
patients get neurofibromas

1025
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:00,240
but they can also develop

1026
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:01,420
pheochromocytomas.

1027
00:25:01,860 --> 00:25:02,640
And so that's an important

1028
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:03,280
association

1029
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,740
for board exams as well.

1030
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:05,980
And that concludes

1031
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:06,980
both this section

1032
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:08,720
as well as the endocrine chapter.

